Definition
Interview Definition

A System Call is a mechanism through which a user-level program requests services from the Operating System Kernel.

Easy Definition

System Call = A request made by an application to the OS.

Real-Life Example

Imagine a bank.

Customer:

Need money

Can he directly enter vault?

No.

Instead:

Customer
 ↓
Request Form
 ↓
Bank Employee
 ↓
Vault

Similarly:

Application
 ↓
System Call
 ↓
Kernel
 ↓
Hardware
Why Do System Calls Exist?

Three main reasons:

1. Security

Applications should not directly control hardware.

2. Resource Management

OS decides:

CPU allocation
RAM allocation
File access
3. Stability

A buggy app should not crash the whole system.

